! ===========================================================================
!  ansys_rect_ff_oop_halfmodel_lob100.inp  --  Mechanical APDL batch deck
!  Rectangular free-free (FFFF) OOP FE ground truth, l/b=1.0 half-model.
!
!  GENERATED 2026-09-02 by copying the validated, already-debugged
!  ansys_rect_ff_oop_halfmodel.inp (l/b=1.5, job 2398617, corrected
!  2026-08-05) and changing ONLY: LOB (geometry), NDIVX (mesh divisions
!  along the length, rescaled to keep the SAME element size as the l/b=1.5
!  deck -- elem size 1/20 of B for mesh1, 1/30 of B for mesh2, i.e.
!  NDIVX = round(2*LOB*20) for mesh1 and round(2*LOB*30) for mesh2 -- and
!  the *CFOPEN output file basenames (tagged _lob100 so this deck's output
!  files don't collide with the l/b=1.5 deck's or the other new geometry's
!  when run from the same NewAnsys/ directory). The *VWRITE/*DO structure,
!  half-model mirror-BC setup (SYMM/ASYM parity passes), material constants,
!  and Lambda<->Hz conversion (KFAC) are BYTE-IDENTICAL to the validated
!  l/b=1.5 deck -- this file was produced by a scripted find/replace on
!  those 3 items only, not hand-retyped, specifically to avoid
!  reintroducing the known *VWRITE-inside-a-*DO-loop trap this project has
!  hit (and fixed) twice before in other decks.
!
!  REFRAMED FROM THE l/b=1.5 DECK'S OWN HEADER (P5 Phase A audit,
!  2026-09-02, LESSONS_LEARNED Sec 18.75/18.76): the l/b=1.5 deck's own
!  "SOLVER-SIDE REFERENCE TABLE" / "PRE-REGISTERED READING" sections
!  compared against SIX specific candidate Lambda values from a since-
!  RETIRED, ad-hoc 2026-07 corner formula -- not this project's current
!  bc='free_free' corner_ff term (confirmed 2026-09-02 to be identically
!  zero as deployed) nor the untested-at-scale FIX candidate derived the
!  same day. Neither of those has any confirmed candidate Lambda list at
!  l/b=1.0 yet (that is exactly what the Step 4 cluster rescan,
!  submit_rect_ff_p5phaseA_rescan.sh, was launched to produce, in parallel
!  with this deck, for CURRENT and FIX at l/b=1.0/1.5/2.5, both SYM/ANTI).
!  So THIS deck makes NO candidate-comparison claim -- it is deliberately
!  formula-agnostic: extract the genuine FE mode list for a free-free
!  rectangular plate at l/b=1.0, both parities, mesh-converged, and leave
!  the comparison against solver candidates for whichever formula (CURRENT,
!  FIX, or a future replacement) the Step 4 job's output and any later
!  corner re-derivation settle on. Read this deck's raw Lambda_FE list
!  alongside that job's checkpoint files once both are available -- do not
!  assume either the old six-candidate list or this session's FIX candidate
!  is what you're checking against.
!
!  GEOMETRY/MATERIAL (same convention as every other deck in this family):
!    half-breadth B=1.0 m, aspect ratio l/b=1.0 (full length 2.0 m,
!    full breadth 2.0 m), full thickness H=0.04 m (H/(2B)=0.02, thin-plate
!    valid), E=210 GPa, nu=0.30, rho=7800 kg/m^3.
!
!  Lambda -> Hz CONVERSION: identical KFAC derivation to the l/b=1.5 deck
!  (Seok/Tiersten/Scarton 2004 rect Part 1 Eqs.24-28,37-38,41-42) --
!  KFAC = (pi*(H/2))/(4*B^2) * sqrt(G/(6*rho*(1-nu))), independent of LOB,
!  so unchanged from the validated deck.
!
!  WHY A HALF-MODEL / mirror BC pattern: unchanged from the l/b=1.5 deck --
!  SYMM (UY=0,ROTX=0,ROTZ=0) matches solver phin=pi/2 (SYM, even);
!  ASYM (UX=0,UZ=0,ROTY=0) matches solver phin=0 (ANTI, odd).
!
!  READING THIS DECK'S OUTPUT:
!    0. CONVERGENCE GATE FIRST: mesh1 vs mesh2 Lambda_FE lists (same parity
!       pass) must agree <0.3% before reading anything else.
!    1. Discard near-zero (rigid body) entries and anything with Lambda_FE
!       implying f>30 Hz (membrane-mode window, per the l/b=1.5 deck's own
!       mode-family assumption -- unchanged physics, just a different L).
!    2. Compare the surviving SYMM-pass Lambda_FE list against SYM
!       candidates, ASYM-pass against ANTI candidates ONLY -- cross-parity
!       matches do not count -- once those candidate lists exist for this
!       l/b from the Step 4 job / later corner-formula work.
!    EXPLORATORY. No SOLVER_VERSION action, no table promotion from this
!    deck alone regardless of outcome.
!
!  Run headless (matches project convention, 8 CPU shared-memory) --
!  or, preferably, via the Ansys/NewAnsys/ queue (see submit_ansys_queue.sh
!  / ansys_queue_manifest.txt) alongside the other new-geometry deck, since
!  this project has exactly one ANSYS license seat:
!    mapdl -b -smp -np 8 -i ansys_rect_ff_oop_halfmodel_lob100.inp -o ansys_rect_ff_oop_halfmodel_lob100_out.txt
!  Outputs: rect_ff_symm_mesh1_lob100.txt, rect_ff_symm_mesh2_lob100.txt,
!           rect_ff_asym_mesh1_lob100.txt, rect_ff_asym_mesh2_lob100.txt
! ===========================================================================

! ======================= PASS SYMM, mesh1 =======================
FINISH
/CLEAR,NOSTART
/TITLE, rect half-model FFFF l/b=1.0 -- SYMM cut BC, mesh1

B      = 1.0
LOB    = 1.0
L      = LOB*B
H      = 0.04
E_iso  = 210.0e9
NU_iso = 0.30
RHO    = 7800.0
NDIVX  = 40
NDIVY  = 20
NMODES = 30
PI     = 3.14159265358979

/PREP7
ET, 1, SHELL281
SECTYPE, 1, SHELL
SECDATA, H, 1
MP, EX,1,E_iso $ MP, EY,1,E_iso $ MP, EZ,1,E_iso
MP, PRXY,1,NU_iso $ MP, PRYZ,1,NU_iso $ MP, PRXZ,1,NU_iso
GG = E_iso/(2*(1+NU_iso))
MP, GXY,1,GG $ MP, GYZ,1,GG $ MP, GXZ,1,GG
MP, DENS,1,RHO
RECTNG, -L, L, 0, B
TYPE,1 $ SECNUM,1 $ MAT,1
LSEL, S, LOC, Y, 0  $ LSEL, A, LOC, Y, B
LESIZE, ALL, , , NDIVX
LSEL, S, LOC, X, -L $ LSEL, A, LOC, X, L
LESIZE, ALL, , , NDIVY
ALLSEL, ALL
MSHKEY, 1 $ AMESH, ALL
! mirror cut at Y=0: SYMM (even) pattern in GLOBAL Cartesian (Y already the
! mirror-normal axis, Z the shell normal -- no local CS needed)
NSEL, S, LOC, Y, 0
D, ALL, UY, 0 $ D, ALL, ROTX, 0 $ D, ALL, ROTZ, 0
ALLSEL, ALL
FINISH

/SOLU
ANTYPE, MODAL
MODOPT, LANB, NMODES, -1.0, , , ON
MXPAND, NMODES, , , YES
SOLVE
FINISH

/POST1
GG2   = E_iso/(2*(1+NU_iso))
KFAC  = (PI*(H/2))/(4*B*B) * SQRT(GG2/(6*RHO*(1-NU_iso)))
*DIM, FRS1, ARRAY, NMODES
*DIM, MIDX, ARRAY, NMODES
*DIM, LFEA, ARRAY, NMODES
*DO, I, 1, NMODES
  *GET, FRS1(I), MODE, I, FREQ
  MIDX(I) = I
  LFEA(I) = FRS1(I)/KFAC
*ENDDO
! FIXED 2026-09-06: single whole-array *VWRITE call -- NEVER *VWRITE
! inside a *DO loop. The old per-iteration-scalar *VWRITE call this
! replaced silently garbled its own output (confirmed: this exact
! block's Lambda_FE column was all-zero on disk with non-monotonic
! mode numbering before this fix). See project memory
! ansys-kfac-runtime-bug.md and paper2-literature-review-gap-2026-09-05.md.
*CFOPEN, rect_ff_symm_mesh1_lob100, txt
*VWRITE
('mode      f[Hz]           Lambda_FE    (SYMM=EVEN parity; SHELL281 x60/y20; discard ~0Hz rigid + >30Hz likely-membrane)')
*VWRITE, MIDX(1), FRS1(1), LFEA(1)
(F4.0, 3X, E14.6, 3X, F12.6)
*CFCLOS
FINISH

! ======================= PASS SYMM, mesh2 =======================
FINISH
/CLEAR,NOSTART
/TITLE, rect half-model FFFF l/b=1.0 -- SYMM cut BC, mesh2 (convergence)

B      = 1.0
LOB    = 1.0
L      = LOB*B
H      = 0.04
E_iso  = 210.0e9
NU_iso = 0.30
RHO    = 7800.0
NDIVX  = 60
NDIVY  = 30
NMODES = 30
PI     = 3.14159265358979

/PREP7
ET, 1, SHELL281
SECTYPE, 1, SHELL
SECDATA, H, 1
MP, EX,1,E_iso $ MP, EY,1,E_iso $ MP, EZ,1,E_iso
MP, PRXY,1,NU_iso $ MP, PRYZ,1,NU_iso $ MP, PRXZ,1,NU_iso
GG = E_iso/(2*(1+NU_iso))
MP, GXY,1,GG $ MP, GYZ,1,GG $ MP, GXZ,1,GG
MP, DENS,1,RHO
RECTNG, -L, L, 0, B
TYPE,1 $ SECNUM,1 $ MAT,1
LSEL, S, LOC, Y, 0  $ LSEL, A, LOC, Y, B
LESIZE, ALL, , , NDIVX
LSEL, S, LOC, X, -L $ LSEL, A, LOC, X, L
LESIZE, ALL, , , NDIVY
ALLSEL, ALL
MSHKEY, 1 $ AMESH, ALL
NSEL, S, LOC, Y, 0
D, ALL, UY, 0 $ D, ALL, ROTX, 0 $ D, ALL, ROTZ, 0
ALLSEL, ALL
FINISH

/SOLU
ANTYPE, MODAL
MODOPT, LANB, NMODES, -1.0, , , ON
MXPAND, NMODES, , , YES
SOLVE
FINISH

/POST1
GG2   = E_iso/(2*(1+NU_iso))
KFAC  = (PI*(H/2))/(4*B*B) * SQRT(GG2/(6*RHO*(1-NU_iso)))
*DIM, FRS2, ARRAY, NMODES
*DIM, MIDX, ARRAY, NMODES
*DIM, LFEA, ARRAY, NMODES
*DO, I, 1, NMODES
  *GET, FRS2(I), MODE, I, FREQ
  MIDX(I) = I
  LFEA(I) = FRS2(I)/KFAC
*ENDDO
! FIXED 2026-09-06: single whole-array *VWRITE call -- NEVER *VWRITE
! inside a *DO loop. The old per-iteration-scalar *VWRITE call this
! replaced silently garbled its own output (confirmed: this exact
! block's Lambda_FE column was all-zero on disk with non-monotonic
! mode numbering before this fix). See project memory
! ansys-kfac-runtime-bug.md and paper2-literature-review-gap-2026-09-05.md.
*CFOPEN, rect_ff_symm_mesh2_lob100, txt
*VWRITE
('mode      f[Hz]           Lambda_FE    (SYMM=EVEN parity; SHELL281 x90/y30; must agree with x60/y20 <0.3%)')
*VWRITE, MIDX(1), FRS2(1), LFEA(1)
(F4.0, 3X, E14.6, 3X, F12.6)
*CFCLOS
FINISH

! ======================= PASS ASYM, mesh1 =======================
FINISH
/CLEAR,NOSTART
/TITLE, rect half-model FFFF l/b=1.0 -- ASYM cut BC, mesh1

B      = 1.0
LOB    = 1.0
L      = LOB*B
H      = 0.04
E_iso  = 210.0e9
