GG2   = E_iso/(2*(1+NU_iso))
KFAC  = (PI*(H/2))/(4*B*B) * SQRT(GG2/(6*RHO*(1-NU_iso)))
*DIM, FRA2, ARRAY, NMODES
*DIM, MIDX, ARRAY, NMODES
*DIM, LFEA, ARRAY, NMODES
*DO, I, 1, NMODES
  *GET, FRA2(I), MODE, I, FREQ
  MIDX(I) = I
  LFEA(I) = FRA2(I)/KFAC
*ENDDO
! FIXED 2026-09-06: single whole-array *VWRITE call -- NEVER *VWRITE
! inside a *DO loop. The old per-iteration-scalar *VWRITE call this
! replaced silently garbled its own output (confirmed: this exact
! block's Lambda_FE column was all-zero on disk with non-monotonic
! mode numbering before this fix). See project memory
! ansys-kfac-runtime-bug.md and paper2-literature-review-gap-2026-09-05.md.
*CFOPEN, rect_ff_asym_mesh2_lob100, txt
*VWRITE
('mode      f[Hz]           Lambda_FE    (ASYM=ODD parity; SHELL281 x90/y30; must agree with x60/y20 <0.3%)')
*VWRITE, MIDX(1), FRA2(1), LFEA(1)
(F4.0, 3X, E14.6, 3X, F12.6)
*CFCLOS
FINISH
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!  AFTER RUNNING (order matters -- see PRE-REGISTERED READING in header):
!   0. Convergence gate per pass (<0.3%, mesh1 vs mesh2).
!   1. Compare SYMM pass Lambda_FE list against solver SYM candidates
!      (0.056, 0.412, 0.431, 0.864, ~0.96); ASYM pass against the ANTI
!      candidate (0.475) only. Cross-parity matches do not count.
!   2. Discard near-zero (rigid body) entries and anything with
!      Lambda_FE implying f>30 Hz (see mode-family assumption above --
!      spot check one such mode's shape before discounting if unsure).
!   3. If all six miss by a common factor, suspect the KFAC derivation
!      before the physics.
! ===========================================================================
